2. Third-party runtime dependencies
   --------------------------------
   NMAFC depends on third-party packages distributed under their own terms,
   including (non-exhaustive): pydantic, lancedb, pyarrow, numpy, tomli,
   openai, anthropic, boto3, psycopg2-binary, fastapi, uvicorn, websockets,
   rich, python-dotenv, mcp, huggingface-hub, pandas, plotly, kaleido,
   rouge-score.

   `uv.lock` is the authoritative resolved dependency set and should be
   regenerated (`uv lock`) before any release. As of the licensing commit it
   was stale and did not include the `mcp` package.

   No third-party code is vendored into this repository. The `registry/`,
   `patchers/`, `skills/` and `plugins/` paths are customer-supplied runtime
   content, bind-mounted read-only into agent containers, and are not
   distributed as part of the NMAFC source distribution.